\title{Re-reading \em{The Goblin Emperor}}
\date{2026-02-28T22:09:38Z}

\p{This week I've re-read Katherine Addison's \em{The Goblin Emperor} for the third time.  It's not the kind of thing I usually read; I usually can't stand a lot of politics (for example, I found Kim Stanley Robinson's Mars trilogy tiresome at times).  But there is something so wholesome and inspiring about a character who has a lot of power but works very hard to Do The Right Thing in the midst of a system rife with corruption and greed.}

\p{The week before, I read the third book in the spin-off \em{Chronicles of Osreth} trilogy, \em{The Tomb of Dragons}. I enjoy them for similar reasons to \em{The Goblin Emperor}, and I also enjoy the more mystery/detective slant.  I thought I had already read the first two books in the series, but it turns out that I only read the first—oops!  There were multiple references in the third book to things I didn't remember, which I initially chalked up to having read the second book too long ago, but it turns out it was because I actually haven't read it at all.  So I decided I will go back and re-read the first book (\em{Witness for the Dead}) before reading the second, but then I figured I might as well go all the way back and re-read \em{The Goblin Emperor} first.}
